    "section_kx_output_md": "████████████████████████████ DEPTH 0 INPUT PIPELINE: ATTENTION & DECODING ████████████████████████████\n\n📂 Scene: A consulting war room kicks off a new project. Analysts (tokens) are assigned, ready to collaborate on building a client deck. But first, they need context.\n\n🔤 Tokens → 🔢 Embeddings  \n→ Each analyst (token) is handed a briefing (embedding): coordinates describing their relationships to every other analyst, slide, or idea.  \n→ **Analogy:** New hires receive onboarding materials-giving them a broad sense of their project context, but not yet the full story.\n\n        ↓  \n\n🎯 Self-Attention (Q·K → weighted V)  \n→ Analysts begin interacting, asking each other: \"Who else here has information that's relevant to my slide?\" (Q·K). Once identified, they pull key insights (V) into their own notes.  \n→ **Analogy:** Analysts interview colleagues, gathering relevant notes and insights to inform their individual slides.\n\n🧩 Multi-Head Attention  \n→ Multiple analysts simultaneously review the same briefing from different specialized angles (heads): compliance, structure, narrative, risk, and client voice.  \n→ **Analogy:** A partner assigns multiple analysts to the same content, each specifically looking through their unique lens.\n\n📊 Head Bias  \n→ Eventually, one analyst’s angle dominates the narrative-often due to a significant finding, like an identified risk or crucial insight.  \n→ **Analogy:** If the \"risk\" analyst spots a serious issue, everyone pivots their attention to that perspective immediately.\n\n🛠️ **Toggle Embeds at Depth 0:**  \n- 🌡️ `TEMPERATURE = 0` → Strictly deterministic, no creative leaps.  \n   → **Analogy:** Analysts must produce predictable, risk-free content-no surprises allowed.  \n- 🔢 `TOP_K`, 🧮 `TOP_P` = OFF  \n   → Analysts select only the top-ranked interpretation of every point; no alternative ideas allowed.  \n   → **Analogy:** No brainstorming permitted; only the safest, highest-ranked solutions can move forward.\n\n🎬 Final Result of Input Pipeline: A single coherent viewpoint emerges from this collective review, clearly defining the focus of the deck. \n\n-\n\n████████████████████████████ DEPTH 0: GENERAL ANALYST DECK (CoT line cap = s slides) ████████████████████████████\n\n🧑 💼 With the main focus defined, the generalist analyst now crafts the initial draft-a linear, logically coherent set of slides.\n\n📄 Slide 1: [GA Slide 1 Placeholder]  \n...  \n📄 Slide s: [GA Slide s Placeholder]  \n\n🛠️ **Toggle Embed:**  \n- `COT = true` → Chain-of-Thought reasoning activated.  \n  → Analyst must logically sequence each slide, clearly moving from \"Problem\" to \"Insight\" to \"Solution.\"  \n  → **Analogy:** Like creating a logical narrative spine in a consulting deck-no gaps or logical leaps.\n\n🔒 Initial QA Tollgate:  \n✅ Deck undergoes a structural integrity check: slides must be present, logically connected, and clear.  \n🚨 If any slide fails, the deck is immediately blocked and returned for revision.\n\n📦 **Summary:**  \n- The general analyst deck sets the stable foundation.  \n- Deterministic and cautious by design-no creativity or risk-taking at this stage.  \n- It's built to be refined downstream-not replaced.\n\n-\n\n████████████████████████████ DEPTH 1: SPECIALIST ANALYST DECKS (ToT branches) ████████████████████████████\n\n👩 💻 With the General Analyst’s foundational deck now stable, the Partner calls in specialist analysts to probe deeper and uncover fresh perspectives.\n\nEach specialist is given freedom to interpret and challenge the original framing, each through a unique thematic lens.\n\n🛠️ **Toggle Embeds at Depth 1:**\n- 🌡️ `TEMPERATURE > 0` → Specialists are encouraged to explore creative and slightly risky slide ideas.  \n  → **Analogy:** Analysts brainstorm edgy, innovative angles-not just the obvious ones.\n  \n- 🔢 `TOP_K = k` → Specialists choose from the top \"k\" plausible next ideas.  \n  → **Analogy:** Analysts select from the top ideas generated in an internal brainstorm-no idea beyond \"k\" is considered.\n\n- 🧮 `TOP_P = p` → Specialists consider ideas from the top cumulative \"p%\" of ideas ranked by relevance.  \n  → **Analogy:** Analysts draw from the richest pool of ideas, stopping when they've captured the core (top 90% of value).\n\n- 🌳 `TOT = true` → Tree-of-Thought branching activated.  \n  → **Analogy:** Each specialist analyst drafts a small standalone deck, exploring one unique interpretation or \"branch.\"\n\n- `TOT_BRANCH_FACTOR = b` → Number of specialists brought into the room.  \n- `TOT_MAX_DEPTH = d` → Maximum slides each specialist can develop in their variant deck.\n\n📂 **Specialist Deck Assignments:**  \n- Specialist 1 (Compliance lens) → Branch 1:  \n  📄 Slide 1.1: [Placeholder]  \n  ...  \n  📄 Slide 1.d: [Placeholder]\n\n- Specialist 2 (Client Impact lens) → Branch 2:  \n  📄 Slide 2.1: [Placeholder]  \n  ...  \n  📄 Slide 2.d: [Placeholder]\n\n- … Specialist b (Narrative/Structure lens) → Branch b:  \n  📄 Slide b.1: [Placeholder]  \n  ...  \n  📄 Slide b.d: [Placeholder]\n\n👉 **Hybrid Paths Summary:**  \n- Depth 0: 1 General Analyst deck (CoT path)  \n- Depth 1: b Specialist Analyst decks (ToT branches)  \n- Total Hybrid Paths: h = 1 (CoT) + b (ToT branches)\n\n✅ `HYBRID_MIN_PATHS = h`  \n→ Minimum required number of hybrid paths must be met or exceeded to pass.\n\n📦 **Summary:**  \n- Specialists independently explore new angles within clear constraints (no further branching).  \n- Results yield diverse interpretations ready for management evaluation.\n\n-\n\n████████████████████████████ DEPTH 2: SENIOR MANAGER REVIEW (Reflexion) ████████████████████████████\n\n👔 A Senior Manager enters to rigorously audit the General and Specialist decks.\n\n📂 **First Round (Critique & Redlines):**  \n- The Manager scrutinizes each deck (1 CoT + b ToT), marking issues for clarity, accuracy, consistency, and compliance.  \n→ **Analogy:** Like a meticulous partner conducting the first line-by-line review before a major client meeting.\n\n🔄 **Feedback Loop:**  \n- Specialists and the general analyst immediately revise based on Manager’s redlines.  \n- No new creative ideas allowed-only issue-specific corrections.\n\n📂 **Second Round (Validation):**  \n- Manager revisits revised decks, ensuring all requested fixes were accurately implemented.  \n→ **Analogy:** Partner returns for a final walkthrough, confirming that all redlines were addressed exactly as noted.\n\n🛠️ **Toggle Embeds:**  \n- `REFLEXION = true` → Enables critical self-review cycles.  \n- `REFLEXION_ROUNDS = r` → Number of critique & validation iterations. Typically 2 rounds: initial critique and confirmation review.\n\n🔒 **Manager QA Tollgate:**  \n✅ All identified fixes must be accurately implemented.  \n✅ Deck consistency and compliance must pass strict standards.  \n→ If not fully satisfied, the manager blocks and requests additional revisions.\n\n📦 **Summary:**  \n- Reflexion ensures quality and coherence of output decks.  \n- Manager’s approval is mandatory before escalation to partners.\n\n-\n\n████████████████████████████ DEPTH 2: PARTNER POLL (Self-Consistency Voting) ████████████████████████████\n\n🧑 ⚖️ With manager approval secured, decks now move to the Partner level. Each Partner receives a slightly varied \"mini-deck\" combining elements from General Analyst, Specialists, and Manager-approved edits.\n\n📂 **Deck Distribution:**  \n- Each partner gets a unique perspective-some emphasizing strategy, others compliance, others clarity.  \n→ **Analogy:** Partners independently review customized 4-slide executive summary decks without cross-communication.\n\n🛠️ **Toggle Embeds:**  \n- `SELF_CONSISTENCY = true` → Independent voting across decks occurs.  \n- `SC_K = k` → Total number of partners reviewing and voting.  \n- `majority_required = true` → Deck advances only with clear majority support (at least ⌈k/2⌉).\n\n🗳️ **Partner Voting Results:**  \n- ✅ PASS → Majority support obtained; the deck proceeds.  \n- ❌ FAIL → Insufficient agreement triggers regeneration and re-voting.\n\n⚠️ **Dissent & Risk Logging:**  \n- Any dissenting views or risk flags are carefully noted and included as annotations for client transparency.\n\n📦 **Summary:**  \n- Ensures robustness through multiple independent expert reviews.  \n- Only partner-endorsed content advances to final assembly.\n\n-\n\n████████████████████████████ DEPTH 3: CHOSEN PATH (Final Client Deck) ████████████████████████████\n\n🏆 **Final Assembly & Lock-In:**  \n- With Partner consensus established, all validated elements (General Analyst, Specialists, Manager, Partners) are integrated into a single coherent client-ready deck.\n\n🔒 **Final QA Checks:**  \n✅ Hybrid Path Minimum met  \n✅ Partner Vote Consensus achieved  \n✅ Reflexion Rounds fully completed\n\n🚫 **No further revisions allowed:**  \n- Deck is final, locked, and ready for client presentation.\n\n📦 **Summary:**  \n- Final deck reflects robust scrutiny and multi-layer validation.  \n- Ready for client delivery with full confidence in accuracy, coherence, and compliance.\n\n-\n\n████████████████████████████ TRANSFORMER METRICS OVERLAY ████████████████████████████\n\n📊 **Technical Monitoring Throughout the Process:**  \n- 🌡️ **Temperature:** Controls the balance between creativity and safety (risk-taking versus deterministic selection).  \n- 🔢 **Top-K:** Limits selection of top-ranked candidates at each decision point.  \n- 🧮 **Top-P:** Ensures selection from the richest cumulative set of high-quality ideas.  \n- 📈 **Attention Sharpness:** Measures how clearly and consistently focus was maintained on key points.  \n- 🧩 **Head Diversity:** Ensures multiple perspectives were meaningfully explored.\n- 🗳️ **Partner Consensus:** Final approval rate from independent expert voting.  \n- ⚠️ **Risk & Dissent Tracking:** Captures unresolved tensions, flagged risks, or minority views for transparency.  \n- ✅ **Final Verdict Confidence:** Quantified confidence level from full-layer scrutiny.\n\n📦 **Summary:**  \n- Provides a transparent, data-driven overview ensuring decision clarity and confidence for all stakeholders.\n\n-\n\n",
